# Wiz

> Wiz is a cloud and AI security platform that helps organizations protect everything they build and run, from the first line of code through production.

## Academy

Evergreen educational content on cloud and AI security topics, written for security and engineering practitioners.

- [CNAPP 101: An Intro to Cloud Native Application Protection Platforms](https://www.wiz.io/academy/cloud-security/what-is-a-cloud-native-application-protection-platform-cnapp): Foundational guide to cloud native application protection platforms, what they are, how they work, and why they matter.
- [What is AI-APP? A security guide to AI Application Protection Platforms](https://www.wiz.io/academy/ai-security/ai-app-ai-application-protection-platform): Introduces the AI-APP category and explains how organizations can secure AI applications from code to runtime.
- [What is API Security? Risks, Standards, and FAQs](https://www.wiz.io/academy/api-security/what-is-api-security): Covers the strategies, procedures, and solutions used to defend APIs against threats, vulnerabilities, and unauthorized access.
- [What Is Application Security? AppSec Uses, Tools, and Tips](https://www.wiz.io/academy/application-security/what-is-application-security): Overview of how organizations identify, mitigate, and protect applications from vulnerabilities throughout the development lifecycle.
- [Data Security: The Ultimate Resource Hub](https://www.wiz.io/academy/data-security): Resource hub covering how organizations protect sensitive data across cloud, SaaS, and AI systems, including classification, governance, and end-to-end security.
- [Cloud Compliance 101: Regulations and Best Practices](https://www.wiz.io/academy/compliance/cloud-compliance-fast-track-guide): Guide to cloud compliance regulations and best practices for security and engineering teams.
- [What is Container Security?](https://www.wiz.io/academy/container-security/what-is-container-security): Covers the processes and tools required to protect containerized applications and their environments from security threats.
- [What Is Cloud Cost?](https://www.wiz.io/academy/cloud-cost/what-are-cloud-costs): Overview of total cloud spend across compute, storage, networking, licensing, and third-party services in public cloud environments.
- [Threat Intelligence: Types, Lifecycle, and Use Cases](https://www.wiz.io/academy/threat-intel/what-is-threat-intelligence): Explains the systematic collection and analysis of data about current and emerging cyber threats to help organizations make informed security decisions.
- [What is Vulnerability Management?](https://www.wiz.io/academy/vulnerability-management/what-is-vulnerability-management): Covers the continuous process of finding, prioritizing, and fixing security weaknesses before attackers can exploit them.
- [Threat Detection and Response (TDR) Explained](https://www.wiz.io/academy/detection-and-response/threat-detection-and-response-tdr): Explains how TDR combines continuous monitoring, threat identification, investigation, and containment to find and stop attacks before they cause damage.
- [What is AI Security? Securing Models, Agents & Data](https://www.wiz.io/academy/what-is-ai-security): Covers the dual practice of using AI tools for cybersecurity and protecting AI systems themselves, including models, pipelines, and the data they touch.
- [What is CSPM? Cloud Security Posture Management](https://www.wiz.io/academy/cloud-security/what-is-cloud-security-posture-management-cspm): Explains how CSPM tools continuously monitor cloud configurations to identify and remediate risks and misconfigurations across IaaS, PaaS, and SaaS environments.
- [Model Context Protocol Security Explained](https://www.wiz.io/academy/ai-security/model-context-protocol-security): Covers how MCP creates direct pathways between AI systems and enterprise resources, the security risks that introduces, and how to secure MCP implementations.

