## Solutions

Wiz solution pages covering specific security capabilities and use cases.

- [AI Security Posture Management (AI-SPM)](https://www.wiz.io/solutions/ai-spm): Secures AI applications with continuous visibility and proactive risk mitigation across models, training data, and AI services.
- [Vulnerability Management](https://www.wiz.io/solutions/vulnerability-management): Unified vulnerability management across cloud workloads, containers, and code, prioritized by real exploitability and business context.
- [Cloud Security Posture Management (CSPM)](https://www.wiz.io/solutions/cspm): Continuously monitors cloud configurations to identify and remediate misconfigurations and risks across IaaS, PaaS, and SaaS environments.
- [Cloud Infrastructure Entitlement Management (CIEM)](https://www.wiz.io/solutions/ciem): Manages cloud identities and entitlements to reduce overprivileged access and eliminate identity-based attack paths.
- [Exposure Management](https://www.wiz.io/solutions/exposure-management): Continuously discovers and reduces the external attack surface by identifying and prioritizing exposed assets and risks.
- [Attack Surface Management (ASM)](https://www.wiz.io/solutions/asm): Discovers internet-facing assets, APIs, and identities to give security teams a complete view of their external exposure.
- [Data Security Posture Management (DSPM)](https://www.wiz.io/solutions/dspm): Discovers and protects sensitive data across cloud environments, identifying where data is exposed, who can access it, and how it flows.
- [Cloud Compliance](https://www.wiz.io/solutions/compliance): Automates compliance monitoring and reporting across frameworks including SOC 2, PCI DSS, HIPAA, NIST, and CIS Benchmarks.
- [Infrastructure-as-Code (IaC) Scanning](https://www.wiz.io/solutions/iac): Scans IaC templates to catch misconfigurations and security issues before they reach production.
- [WizOS: Secured Container Images](https://www.wiz.io/solutions/wizos): Hardened, minimal container base images that reduce the attack surface and eliminate unnecessary packages from the start.
- [Static Application Security Testing (SAST)](https://www.wiz.io/solutions/sast): Analyzes source code to detect security vulnerabilities early in the development lifecycle.
- [Supply Chain Security](https://www.wiz.io/solutions/supply-chain-security): Identifies vulnerabilities and risks across open source dependencies, third-party packages, and the software supply chain.
- [Application Security Posture Management (ASPM)](https://www.wiz.io/solutions/aspm): Connects code, cloud, and runtime context to give security and development teams a unified view of application risk.
- [Cloud Workload Protection Platform (CWPP)](https://www.wiz.io/solutions/cwpp): Protects cloud workloads including VMs, containers, and serverless functions with agentless visibility and runtime security.
- [Runtime Sensor](https://www.wiz.io/solutions/runtime-sensor): Provides deep runtime visibility into workload behavior, processes, and network activity for threat detection and response.
- [Container & Kubernetes Security](https://www.wiz.io/solutions/container-and-kubernetes-security): Secures containers and Kubernetes environments with visibility into misconfigurations, vulnerabilities, and runtime threats.
- [Cloud Cost](https://www.wiz.io/solutions/cloud-cost): Helps organizations understand and optimize cloud spend across compute, storage, networking, and third-party services.

